<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gezira Scheme</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gezira">Gezira</a> Scheme is a large irrigation project on the Gezira plain between the Blue and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-nile">White Niles</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, opened in 1925 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Sennar</a> Dam was completed. Run as a partnership between the government, a British company and tenant farmers, it grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> for export and became the backbone of the Sudanese economy. It remains one of the largest irrigation schemes in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gezira-scheme.jpg" alt="Gezira Scheme" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sudan_Gezira_Plain_1997.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
